"""Definitions for the 183 food categories (docs/CATEGORIES.md): the instructions an AI classifier will follow.

Each entry: code -> {"d": definition, "inc": typical members, "exc": what does NOT belong, with the right code}.
Placement of borderline foods follows USDA's own FNDDS → WWEIA assignments where USDA has them (checked
2026-11-16 against work/reference/wweia_2021_2023.xlsx); deviations are marked "(differs from USDA)".
Rendered by tools/categories/build_definitions.py.
"""

GLOBAL_RULES = [
    ("One category", "Every product gets exactly one category: the one that best describes what the product **is**, as sold (packaged foods) or as eaten (dishes)."),
    ("Processing is a tag", "Fresh, frozen, canned, dried, raw or cooked do **not** change the category (frozen broccoli → 6407, canned peaches → 6008). Record the state as a tag. Exception: dried fruit has its own category (6016)."),
    ("Uncooked staples", "Dry or uncooked staples go to the category of the food they become: dry pasta → 4004, dry rice → 4002, dried lentils → 2802, rolled oats → 4802."),
    ("Ready meals and kits", "Ready meals, frozen meals and meal kits go to the dish they make: frozen pizza → 3602, lasagna → 3204, taco kit → 3502, risotto kit → 3202."),
    ("Single food vs dish", "A single food with only seasoning, marinade or sauce stays in its own category (marinated chicken breast → 2202, tuna in oil → 2402). Combined with other foods (pasta, rice, vegetables, bread) it becomes a dish (31xx–38xx)."),
    ("Sandwiches and wraps", "Sandwiches, wraps and subs go to the 37xx category of their **main filling**."),
    ("Use the nutrition values", "Some categories split on nutrients; use the product's values per 100 g / 100 ml. **Milk fat**: whole ≥ 3.0 g, reduced fat 1.8–2.9 g, lowfat 0.6–1.7 g (incl. European semi-skimmed 1.5 %), nonfat < 0.6 g; unknown → reduced fat. **Ready-to-eat cereal**: sugars > 21.2 g → 4602, otherwise 4604. **Diet drinks** (71xx): ≤ 1 g sugars per 100 ml and sweetened with non-nutritive sweeteners (\"zero\", \"diet\", \"light\", \"sugar-free\")."),
    ("Biscuit", "\"Biscuit\" means a cookie in UK/European usage (→ 5504) but a bread-like quick bread in US usage (→ 4402). Decide from the product, not the word."),
    ("Plant-based alternatives", "Milk alternatives → 1902, yogurt alternatives → 1904, meat / cheese / other alternatives → 2806, ice cream alternatives → 5802 (differs from USDA)."),
    ("Survey-only categories", "6489 *Vegetables on a sandwich*, 7702 *Tap water* and 9602 *Human milk* exist only for diet surveys. **Never** assign them to a product."),
    ("Last resort", "9999 *Not included in a food category* only for non-food items (pet food, cosmetics, cutlery) or a food that truly fits no definition. Target: < 1 % of products."),
]

